# Build context for docker/Dockerfile.
#
# Allowlist: ignore everything, then re-include only what the image needs.
# Anything new at the top level of the repo (papers, datasets, vendor SDKs,
# editor folders) therefore stays out of the image without touching this file.

*

!docker/
!fic_library/
!fic_ws/src/
!Extensions/
!fic_docs/
!docs/scripting/
!fic_api/
!fic_install/fic-control-studio.svg
!README.md

# ── Re-exclude within the allowed trees ─────────────────────────────────────

# Host build artefacts: colcon bakes absolute paths into them and they are
# built for the host's architecture. The image builds its own.
fic_ws/src/*/build
fic_ws/src/*/install
fic_ws/src/*/log
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store

# Newton needs an NVIDIA GPU with CUDA, which Docker Desktop cannot provide.
# Leaving it out means the Studio never offers it (it falls back to MuJoCo).
fic_ws/src/mujoco_newton


# Output folders of the extensions. At runtime they live in the user's folder.
Extensions/*/plots
Extensions/*/runs
Extensions/*/run_log.json
fic_ws/src/fic_studio/fic_studio/experiments
**/MUJOCO_LOG.TXT
Extensions/alvr_dashboard

# Maintainer output (image tarballs written by docker/build.sh), and the
# default shared folder of docker/compose.yaml (user data).
docker/dist
docker/FIC_Studio
